<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n70158" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νέκυς</span></b>  (
			Lacon.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νέκυρ</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			Hsch.
		</span></i>), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῠος</span>, ὁ,
		poet. dat. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νέκυϊ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					16.526
				</span></i>
			, etc.; 
				Ep.
			 dat. pl. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεκύεσσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					11.491
				</span></i>
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νέκυσσι</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				569
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				22.401
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				23.45
			</span></i>; acc. pl. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νέκῡς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					7.420
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				18.180
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				24.417
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				176.4
			</span></i>; also 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νέκυας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					7.418
				</span></i>
			, al.:—<i>corpse,</i> freq. in <i><span class="en">
				Il.
			</span></i>, less freq. in <i><span class="en">
				Od.
			</span></i>; in <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				4.492
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				493
			</span></i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νέκυς</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεκρός</span> are used of the same dead person; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. ἀνδρός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					1.140
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				3.16
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				24
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				26
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Or.</u>
				1585
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. τεθνηώς, κατατεθνηώς,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				18.173
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				16.526
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νέκυες κατατεθνηῶτες, κτάμενοι,
				καταφθίμενοι,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				10.530
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				23.45
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				11.491
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνδρὸς Πέρσεω ὁ ν.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					1.140
				</span></i>
			, cf.<i><span class="en">
				3.16
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ κατθανὼν ν.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ant.</u>
					515
				</span></i>
			; <i>dead person,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεκύων σώματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					62
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in pl.,
				<i>spirits of the dead,</i> freq. in <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				11
			</span></i>, less freq. in <i><span class="en">
				Il.
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεκύων ἀμενηνὰ κάρηνα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					11.29
				</span></i>
			, cf.<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				15.251
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πεδ᾽ ἀμαύρων ν.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Sapph.
					68
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> as Adj.
			<i>dead,</i> post-<i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐχθρὸν ὧδ᾽ αἰδῇ
			νέκυν</span>; <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				1356
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κίχλαι αἱ νέκυες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					11.96
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Nicarch.
			</span></i>); cf. however <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				24.35
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				423
			</span></i>.—Poet. word, used also by <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
			</span></i>, in <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				22.1672.119
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iv B.C.)</span>, in Cretan, Kohler-Ziebarth <i>Stadtrecht
				von Gortyn</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				p.35
			</span></i>, and in late Prose, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Crass.</u>
				19
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdn.
				4.8.5
			</span></i>. [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῡ</span> of nom. and
			acc. sg. in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				4.492
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				22.386
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῠ</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Simon.
				114.5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				70
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Or.</u>
				1585
			</span></i>, and in later Poets, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				4.480
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Bion
				1.71
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				7.1
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Alc.
			</span></i> Mess.).] (Cf. Avest. <i>nasu-</i> 'corpse', Skt.
				<i>náśyati</i> 'perish', 'disappear',
			Lat. <i>necare.</i>)</div>
